From: xlulx <92148312+xlulx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Skip the SNI context lookup outside tray owners.

NtUserGetCursorPos() reads the cursor from shared memory without a server
call. Since 0001, it first asks sni_get_context_menu_pos() whether a tray
click is being placed, and that reads __wine_sni_context_time from the
desktop window through NtUserGetProp(), which is a get_window_property
server request. Every process pays it on every GetCursorPos(), including
games with no tray icon and sessions with no StatusNotifierWatcher, where
nothing is ever published.

A server trace on an ARM64 handheld (gamescope session, FEX) shows two to
three such requests per frame on the main thread of Unity games: about
150 per second in R.E.P.O. and 100 per second in ULTRAKILL, each returning
OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND. They were the most frequent request from R.E.P.O.'s
main thread.

The context only matters to the process that places a menu at the click,
which is the icon's owner. Shell_NotifyIconW() reaches sni_notify_icon() in
the calling process for every message, so note that call there and skip
the lookup in processes that never made one. Tray owners keep the current
behaviour, and sni_should_layer_context_menu() still reads the published
context for cross-process menus.

A process that shows a menu for an icon another process added, without
calling Shell_NotifyIcon itself, now places it at the real pointer.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sni.c b/dlls/win32u/sni.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/sni.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sni.c
@@ -170,6 +170,7 @@ static pthread_mutex_t sni_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
 static DBusConnection *sni_connection; /* CONTROL connection: watcher tracking + balloons, no items */
 static BOOL sni_available;           /* watcher present and connection up */
 static BOOL sni_init_done;
+static LONG sni_tray_used;           /* this process has made a Shell_NotifyIcon call */
 static int wake_pipe[2] = { -1, -1 }; /* self-pipe: wakes the pump when the connection set changes */
 
 /* Wake the pump thread out of poll() so it rebuilds its connection set (a new
@@ -604,6 +605,10 @@ BOOL sni_get_context_menu_pos( POINT *pos )
 {
     BOOL ret, latched;
 
+    /* Only a tray icon's owner places a menu at its click. Reading the
+     * published context costs a server call on every GetCursorPos. */
+    if (!ReadNoFence( &sni_tray_used )) return FALSE;
+
     pthread_mutex_lock( &sni_mutex );
     /* Override the cursor only while the menu is being placed. A latched (on
      * screen) menu must see the real pointer. */
@@ -1258,6 +1263,8 @@ LRESULT sni_notify_icon( HWND owner, UINT msg, NOTIFYICONDATAW *nid )
     struct sni_icon *icon, *target = NULL;
     LRESULT ret = -1;
 
+    InterlockedExchange( &sni_tray_used, 1 );
+
     /* GNOME's AppIndicator host requires a D-Bus menu and already translates
      * double-clicks into Activate. Use explorer's XEmbed path on Mutter/X11;
      * our native-menu SNI backend cannot preserve those interactions there. */
